marta: Heads-up 1 PR #5123 updates the Go quickstart to show Cloud Run deploy + improved auth pattern. Switching from hardcoded token -> env var + add a tiny migration note for folks moving from SDK v5 -> v6.

lee: Nice. Is this adding a Cloud Run Dockerfile or using the native `gcloud run deploy` flow?

marta: Both: tiny Dockerfile (scratch + distroless) and a `gcloud` snippet that sets REDWOOD_API_KEY as a secret env var.

samir: Can you paste the example handler/snippet so I can check the imports? Go modules are picky.

marta: Sure 1 main.go snippet (keeps deps to stdlib + net/http):

```go
// main.go
package main

import (
  "encoding/json"
  "net/http"
  "os"
)

func handler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
  apiKey := os.Getenv("REDWOOD_API_KEY")
  if apiKey == "" {
    http.Error(w, "missing REDWOOD_API_KEY", http.StatusUnauthorized)
    return
  }
  var req struct{ Input string `json:\"input\"` }
  if err := json.NewDecoder(r.Body).Decode(&req); err != nil {
    http.Error(w, "bad request", http.StatusBadRequest)
    return
  }
  // minimal request to Redwood hosted API
  // NOTE: in prod use a proper HTTP client with timeouts and retry logic
  res, _ := http.Post("https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate", "application/json", r.Body)
  defer res.Body.Close()
  w.WriteHeader(res.StatusCode)
  json.NewDecoder(res.Body).Decode(&map[string]interface{}{})
}

func main() {
  http.HandleFunc("/", handler)
  http.ListenAndServe(":8080", nil)
}
```

claire: Two small things: 1) the snippet reuses r.Body for the forwarded request which will be empty after Decode. We should build a new body buffer. 2) add a callout about setting the Cloud Run env var via `gcloud run deploy --set-env-vars=REDWOOD_API_KEY=...` or use Secret Manager.

marta: Good catch, I'll replace with a buf copy and add Secret Manager suggestion + one-liner migration note for SDK v5->v6 about import path (we renamed the Go client package path).

samir: Also add a troubleshooting note: if you get 403 from Cloud Run, check IAM for the service account and that you didn't accidentally publish the key in the image.

claire: tiny copyedit: in the PR description "CloudRun" -> "Cloud Run" (two words).

